  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_015: scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, weighted; acc=0.713) establishes that multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the dominant architecture. However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as scvi_n200 in this best setting. Since RNA is the dominant signal (RNA-only 0.485 vs image-only 0.208), the choice of RNA representation is the most consequential remaining design decision. Config_024 swaps only the RNA encoder to scgpt while holding all other factors at their best-known values (multiprofile, resnet50, transformer, weighted), giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_015. This directly tests whether a pretrained generative RNA model (scgpt) provides a richer representation than the variational autoencoder (scvi_n200) in the multiprofile regime. If scgpt matches or exceeds scvi_n200, it opens a new direction; if it underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and can redirect exploration toward the image encoder or other factors. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information, most actionable next step."
}

